IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`

-- Stamp Duty Act 1978 (NT) -- conveyance duty on a home, the home concessions and exemptions, and the duties to lodge,
-- pay and notify. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE: the rules are in the Act's own actors and terms ("the conveyee or conveyees", "the
-- Commissioner", "the building contractor"). The individual buyer's questions are in sda-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this
-- module and restates no rule.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. This is not an official version of the Stamp Duty Act 1978. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation
-- is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from reprint REPS013, as in force at 1 July 2025, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/Stamp-Duty-Act-1978-NT-current-reprint-REPS013.txt, under the Northern Territory
-- copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 Oct 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
--
-- THE NORTHERN TERRITORY LEVIES NO LAND TAX. There is no land tax Act in the Territory, so there is no land tax and no
-- principal place of residence exemption from land tax to encode here (unlike Western Australia's
-- land-tax-assessment-act-2002). Council rates and their concessions are not in this Act.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 4 (conveyee, consideration), s 4A(1) (unencumbered value, an INPUT), s 4AB(1) (dutiable value);
-- ss 5, 6 and Schedule 1 cl 1(2) (the conveyance scale; the cl 1(2)(a) formula read as V squared, see NOTES.md) and
-- cl 1(3) (joint tenants, plus $5); s 50(a) and s 9(7) (who is liable); s 9(1), (3), (3A), (5), (6) (lodge within 60
-- days of first execution, pay by the last day for lodgement, as regulative rules); Part 5 Division 2: s 88 (the
-- concession amounts, threshold amount, period for occupancy, prescribed period), s 88A (the Division ends with
-- conveyances first executed on 30 June 2021), ss 89, 89AA, 89AAB, 89AAC, 89A, 90, 90AA (conditions and date windows),
-- s 90A and s 90AB (reassessment when the first home owner grant is paid or not), s 90B (one concession only, the
-- greatest), the notices of failure to occupy (ss 89(3), 89AA(6), 89AAB(7), 89A(3), 90(3), 90D(5)) and the
-- Commissioner's duty to reassess (ss 89(4), 89AAB(4)(b), 89A(6), 90(4), 90D(8)), as regulative rules; s 102 (the 2010
-- amendments start on 4 May 2010); Part 5 Division 2A, ss 90C, 90D (the house-and-land exemption, 1 July 2022 to
-- 30 June 2027); Part 5 Division 3, s 91 (relationship breakdown); Schedule 2 items 6(d), 6(e) and 7.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: corporate reconstructions, partnerships, insurance, trusts and options, landholder duty (Part 3
-- Division 8A), family farms, managed investment schemes, leases, partitions (cl 1(4)-(10)); the replacement and option
-- savings rules of ss 97A, 102(2), 106, 109, 111, 112, 115, 116; guardians (ss 89(7), 89AA(7) and the like) and Housing
-- Act schemes; the Commissioner's discretions to extend or reduce periods, except as facts. The FHOG Act's own tests
-- (whether a conveyee is entitled to a first home owner grant, "home", "relevant interest", "residential property",
-- "permanent resident") are FACTS, as s 88(1) borrows them from the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000.
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Stamp Duty Act 1978 -- conveyance duty on a home, seat-neutral core`

§§ `ss 4, 4A and 4AB -- dutiable value`

-- s 4(1): "consideration, in relation to a conveyance, means the consideration for the conveyance without any
-- deduction or discount for the amount of GST". s 4A(1): "The unencumbered value of property is the full value of the
-- property free from encumbrances (including any GST payable on the supply of the property)" -- a valuation, so an INPUT.
-- s 4AB(1): "(a) if consideration is, or is to be, given for the property -- the amount or value of the consideration or
-- the unencumbered value of the property (whichever is the greater); or (b) if no consideration is given for the
-- property -- the unencumbered value of the property." A consideration of 0 is read as none given.
GIVEN `the consideration` IS A NUMBER, `the unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dutiable value` MEANS
    IF `the consideration` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the greater of` `the consideration` `the unencumbered value`
    ELSE `the unencumbered value`

§§ `ss 5, 6 and Schedule 1 cl 1(2) -- the conveyance scale`

-- s 5(1): "Stamp duty is imposed ... (a) on dutiable instruments". s 6: "The rate of duty is the rate specified in
-- Schedule 1". Schedule 1 cl 1(1): "A conveyance of dutiable property is a dutiable instrument." cl 1(2):
--   (a) if the dutiable value does not exceed $525 000:  D = (0.06571441 x V2) + 15V, "V is 1/1 000 of the dutiable
--       value". The deposit reads "V2": the superscript was lost in conversion. It is V SQUARED: at $525 000 the formula
--       gives $25 987.53 and 4.95% gives $25 987.50, so the two parts of the scale meet (NOTES.md, finding 1). The
--       deposit is not altered.
--   (b) "exceeds $525 000 but is less than $3 000 000, the duty is 4.95% of the dutiable value";
--   (c) "$3 000 000 or more but is less than $5 000 000, the duty is 5.75% of the dutiable value";
--   (d) "$5 000 000 or more, the duty is 5.95% of the dutiable value".
-- Each rate in (b)-(d) applies to the WHOLE dutiable value, not to the part above the threshold.
GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` MEANS
    IF `the dutiable value` AT MOST 525000
    THEN (0.06571441 TIMES `V` TIMES `V`) PLUS (15 TIMES `V`)
    ELSE IF `the dutiable value` LESS THAN 3000000
         THEN `the dutiable value` TIMES 4.95 DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE IF `the dutiable value` LESS THAN 5000000
              THEN `the dutiable value` TIMES 5.75 DIVIDED BY 100
              ELSE `the dutiable value` TIMES 5.95 DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `V` MEANS `the dutiable value` DIVIDED BY 1000

-- TAA s 26(1): a liability "is to be assessed by reference to the provisions of the relevant taxation law as in force
-- when the liability arose". The reprint's endnotes record that Schedule 1 was last amended by No. 13, 2017, s 11,
-- which commenced on 1 July 2017; what it changed is not in the deposit. The scale above is therefore applied only to a
-- conveyance first executed on or after 1 July 2017; before then the answer is `not covered`.
`the first day of the deposited Schedule 1` MEANS YMD 2017 7 1

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposited Schedule 1 applies on` IF
    `the day` `is on or after` `the first day of the deposited Schedule 1`

-- Schedule 1 cl 1(3): "A conveyance of dutiable property by or to joint tenants is, if the conveyor, or one or more of
-- the conveyors, retains an interest in the property, assessed for duty as a conveyance of the interest that is not
-- retained by the conveyor or conveyors rather than the form of the conveyance but an additional $5 is payable."
-- s 4AC(2): "The interest of a joint owner of property is valued as if both or all joint owners were tenants in common
-- in equal shares."
`the joint tenancy surcharge` MEANS 5

-- s 4AC(1): "the value of the interest of an owner in the property is assessed by multiplying the total value of the
-- property by a fraction representing the owner's proportionate share of ownership"; (3): it applies to dutiable value.
GIVEN `the value of the whole property` IS A NUMBER
      `the share, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of a share in property held in common` MEANS
    `the value of the whole property` TIMES `the share, as a fraction`

GIVEN `the dutiable value of the interest not retained` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule 1 cl 1(3) duty on a joint tenancy conveyance` MEANS
    `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` `the dutiable value of the interest not retained` PLUS `the joint tenancy surcharge`

§§ `s 50 and s 9(7) -- who is liable`

-- s 50: "Subject to this Act: (a) duty imposed on a conveyance is payable by the conveyee; and (b) duty imposed on a
-- lease is payable by the lessee." s 9(7): "If this Act does not make a particular party to a dutiable transaction
-- liable for payment of duty on the transaction ..., then all parties are jointly and severally liable".
DECLARE `Kind of dutiable transaction` IS ONE OF
    `a conveyance`
    `a lease`
    `a transaction for which the Act makes no particular party liable`

DECLARE `Who is liable` IS ONE OF
    `the conveyee (s 50(a))`
    `the lessee (s 50(b))`
    `every party, jointly and severally (s 9(7))`

GIVEN `the transaction` IS A `Kind of dutiable transaction`
GIVETH A `Who is liable`
`who is liable for the duty on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the transaction`
    WHEN `a conveyance` THEN `the conveyee (s 50(a))`
    WHEN `a lease` THEN `the lessee (s 50(b))`
    WHEN `a transaction for which the Act makes no particular party liable` THEN `every party, jointly and severally (s 9(7))`

§§ `s 9 -- lodging the instrument and paying the duty (regulative)`

-- s 9(1): "a dutiable instrument must be lodged with the Commissioner for the assessment of duty: (a) within 60 days
-- after it is first executed". (3): the obligation does not extend to a motor vehicle certificate of registration, a
-- policy of insurance, or an instrument exempt under Schedule 2 items 9 to 13 or 15 -- so a conveyance exempt under
-- s 90D, s 91 or Schedule 2 item 6 or 7 must still be lodged. (3A): no obligation "to lodge and pay duty" on a
-- conveyance "that does not proceed" unless there is a sub-sale or a conveyance by direction. (5): duty "must be paid
-- on or before the last day allowed for lodgement of the instrument unless a later date is fixed in a notice of
-- assessment". (6): the person liable "must ensure that: (a) the instrument is lodged ... on or before the last day
-- allowed for its lodgement; and (b) the duty is paid on or before the last day allowed for payment."
-- Clock: days from the day the instrument is first executed.
`the days to lodge a dutiable instrument` MEANS 60

GIVEN `days to the later date fixed in a notice of assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days to pay the duty` MEANS
    `the greater of` `the days to lodge a dutiable instrument` `days to the later date fixed in a notice of assessment`

GIVEN `the conveyance does not proceed, with no sub-sale or conveyance by direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `duty is payable on the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days to the later date fixed in a notice of assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 9 -- lodge within 60 days after first execution, and pay by the last day for lodgement` IS
    IF `the conveyance does not proceed, with no sub-sale or conveyance by direction`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE IF `duty is payable on the conveyance`
         THEN    (PARTY `the conveyee`
                  MUST  `lodge the instrument with the Commissioner for assessment`
                  WITHIN `the days to lodge a dutiable instrument`
                  LEST  BREACH BY `the conveyee` BECAUSE "s 9(1)(a), (6)(a): a dutiable instrument must be lodged with the Commissioner for assessment within 60 days after it is first executed")
             RAND
                 (PARTY `the conveyee`
                  MUST  `pay the duty`
                  WITHIN `the days to pay the duty` `days to the later date fixed in a notice of assessment`
                  LEST  BREACH BY `the conveyee` BECAUSE "s 9(5), (6)(b): duty must be paid on or before the last day for lodgement unless a later date is fixed in the notice of assessment; late payment is a tax default, with interest (TAA s 34) and penalty tax (TAA s 39)")
         ELSE PARTY `the conveyee`
              MUST  `lodge the instrument with the Commissioner for assessment`
              WITHIN `the days to lodge a dutiable instrument`
              LEST  BREACH BY `the conveyee` BECAUSE "s 9(1)(a), (3): an exempt conveyance (other than under Schedule 2 items 9 to 13 or 15) must still be lodged with the Commissioner within 60 days after it is first executed"

§§ `Part 5 Division 2 -- the facts of a home conveyance`

-- s 88(1) "relevant time": when the instrument (or the first of several) is executed -- the date first executed.
-- Each "the Commissioner is satisfied that" is answered conditionally: the fact as the conveyee states it. Terms that
-- s 88(1) takes from the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (Australian citizen, permanent resident, home, relevant
-- interest, residential property, first home owner grant, owner builder, comprehensive home building contract) are
-- FACTS. Where a section asks about "each" conveyee or "at least one", the fact says so.
DECLARE `Home conveyance` HAS
    `the date first executed`                                                         IS A DATE
    `the consideration`                                                               IS A NUMBER
    `the unencumbered value`                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `there is a home on the land at the relevant time`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an off-the-plan contract`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `every conveyee is an individual`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least one conveyee is 18 or older, or is exempted from the age requirement`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least one conveyee is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least one conveyee is 60 or older at the relevant time`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least one conveyee holds an NT pensioner, carer or concession scheme card`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a conveyee or spouse has received the first home owner concession before`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in a residence they occupied`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a conveyee or spouse has received a grant, discount, concession or rebate before, not repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in residential property`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a conveyee or spouse had a relevant interest in Territory residential property in the 24 months before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner exempts that Territory interest for a relationship breakdown`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a conveyee already has a beneficial interest in the land`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conveyees will acquire the whole beneficial interest in the land`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a conveyee will acquire an interest in the land as trustee`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `every conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least one conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a conveyee who is 60 or older or holds a card will occupy the home`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the home has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the home is substantially renovated new residential premises not occupied or sold since` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner declares the home a qualifying home`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a conveyee has been paid, is entitled to or will become entitled to a first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conveyee is paid the grant for a transaction that commenced from 1 January 2015 to 6 May 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conveyees become entitled to possession within 12 months after settlement`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- Glosses. "occupy the home as their principal place of residence" means for the prescribed period (6 months in a row,
-- s 88(1)) beginning within the period for occupancy. "card": an NT Pensioner and Carer Concession Card or a Northern
-- Territory Concession Scheme Card, held at the relevant time (or held at the application, having been entitled to it at
-- the relevant time) -- an administrative scheme, not in statute, so a FACT (NOTES.md, finding 3). "within 12 months
-- after settlement" includes a longer period the Commissioner approves for special reasons.

GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dutiable value of the conveyance` MEANS
    `the dutiable value` (`c`'s `the consideration`) (`c`'s `the unencumbered value`)

§§ `s 88 -- the concessions and their amounts`

DECLARE `Home concession` IS ONE OF
    `the first home owner concession (s 89)`
    `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)`
    `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)`
    `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)`
    `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)`

`all the home concessions` MEANS
    LIST `the first home owner concession (s 89)`,
         `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)`,
         `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)`,
         `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)`,
         `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)`

-- s 88(1) "threshold amount means: (a) an amount prescribed by regulation; or (b) if no amount is prescribed ... --
-- $650 000." No regulation is deposited: the Act's own $650 000 is used (a prescribed amount would change the answers).
`the threshold amount` MEANS 650000

-- s 88(1) "first home owner concession means a concession ... equal to the lesser of: (a) the total amount of duty
-- assessed as payable on the conveyance; or (b) the duty payable on a conveyance of land with a dutiable value of
-- $540 000."
-- "first home owner discount means ...: (a) for a conveyance first executed on or after 24 May 2016 but before
-- 1 September 2016 -- the lesser of: (i) 50% of the duty assessed ...; or (ii) $10 000; or (b) for a conveyance first
-- executed on or after 1 September 2016 but before 7 May 2019, if the dutiable value of the land does not exceed the
-- threshold amount: (i) an amount prescribed by regulation [none deposited]; or (ii) ... the lesser of: (A) the total
-- amount of duty assessed ...; or (B) the duty payable on a conveyance of land with a dutiable value of $500 000; or
-- (c) for a conveyance first executed on or after 1 September 2016 but before 1 January 2017, if the dutiable value of
-- the land exceeds the threshold amount -- $10 000." Above the threshold from 1 January 2017 the definition gives no
-- amount: 0.
-- "senior, pensioner and carer concession means ... the lesser of ... (a) the total amount of duty assessed ...;
-- (b) ... (i) for a conveyance that was first executed before 28 April 2015 -- $8 500; (ii) ... on or after 28 April
-- 2015 -- $10 000."
-- "principal place of residence rebate means ... the lesser of: (a) the total amount of duty assessed ...; or (b) ...
-- (i) ... first executed before 4 December 2012 -- $3 500; (ii) ... on or after 4 December 2012 -- $7 000."
-- "Territory home owner discount means a concession: (a) ... equal to the lesser of: (i) the total amount of duty
-- assessed ...; or (ii) $18 601; and (b) that applies if the dutiable value of the land does not exceed the threshold
-- amount."
GIVEN `the concession` IS A `Home concession`
      `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
      `the duty assessed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the concession`
    WHEN `the first home owner concession (s 89)` THEN
        `the lesser of` `the duty assessed` (`the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 540000)
    WHEN `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` THEN
        IF `the day falls from` `day` `to` (YMD 2016 5 24) `and` (YMD 2016 8 31)
        THEN `the lesser of` (`the duty assessed` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100) 10000
        ELSE IF     `the day falls from` `day` `to` (YMD 2016 9 1) `and` (YMD 2019 5 6)
                AND `the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c` AT MOST `the threshold amount`
             THEN `the lesser of` `the duty assessed` (`the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 500000)
             ELSE IF     `the day falls from` `day` `to` (YMD 2016 9 1) `and` (YMD 2016 12 31)
                     AND `the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c` GREATER THAN `the threshold amount`
                  THEN 10000
                  ELSE 0
    WHEN `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` THEN
        IF `the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c` AT MOST `the threshold amount`
        THEN `the lesser of` `the duty assessed` 18601
        ELSE 0
    WHEN `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` THEN
        `the lesser of` `the duty assessed` (IF `day` `is before` (YMD 2015 4 28) THEN 8500 ELSE 10000)
    WHEN `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` THEN
        `the lesser of` `the duty assessed` (IF `day` `is before` (YMD 2012 12 4) THEN 3500 ELSE 7000)
    WHERE
        `day` MEANS `c`'s `the date first executed`

§§ `s 88A and the date windows of the concessions`

-- s 88A: "Except if otherwise expressly provided, this Division applies to conveyances first executed on or before
-- 30 June 2021." (Inserted by No. 22, 2019, s 9, with ss 89AAB and 89AAC; amended by No. 28, 2020, s 8.)
-- s 89(1A): s 89 "does not apply in relation to a conveyance that was first executed on or after 4 December 2012".
-- s 89AA(1): "a conveyance first executed on or after 24 May 2016 but before 7 May 2019".
-- s 89AAB(1): "a conveyance first executed on or after 8 February 2019" -- a start, no end.
-- s 89A: no date of its own; s 102(1)(a): the 2010 amendments (which inserted s 89A and raised the s 89 and s 90
-- amounts) "apply to a conveyance first executed on or after 4 May 2010".
-- s 90(1AA): s 90 "does not apply in relation to a conveyance that was first executed on or after 8 February 2019".
-- READING (NOTES.md, finding 2): s 89AAB(1) says when s 89AAB begins and is silent on when it ends; it does not
-- "expressly provide" that the Division applies after 30 June 2021. So s 88A closes the Territory home owner discount,
-- and the senior, pensioner and carer concession, which has no end date of its own, with conveyances first executed on
-- 30 June 2021. The contrary reading is one switch below.
`the last day of Part 5 Division 2 (s 88A)` MEANS YMD 2021 6 30

DECIDE `READING: s 89AAB(1) is an express provision displacing s 88A` IS FALSE

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 5 Division 2 applies to a conveyance first executed on` IF
    `the day` `is on or before` `the last day of Part 5 Division 2 (s 88A)`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 5 Division 2 applies to the conveyance (s 88A)` IF
    `Part 5 Division 2 applies to a conveyance first executed on` (`c`'s `the date first executed`)

GIVEN `the concession` IS A `Home concession`
      `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the concession's date window includes the conveyance` IF
    CONSIDER `the concession`
    WHEN `the first home owner concession (s 89)` THEN
            `Part 5 Division 2 applies to the conveyance (s 88A)` `c`
        AND `day` `is before` (YMD 2012 12 4)
    WHEN `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` THEN
            `Part 5 Division 2 applies to the conveyance (s 88A)` `c`
        AND `day` `is on or after` (YMD 2016 5 24)
        AND `day` `is before` (YMD 2019 5 7)
    WHEN `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` THEN
            (`Part 5 Division 2 applies to the conveyance (s 88A)` `c` OR `READING: s 89AAB(1) is an express provision displacing s 88A`)
        AND `day` `is on or after` (YMD 2019 2 8)
    WHEN `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` THEN
            `Part 5 Division 2 applies to the conveyance (s 88A)` `c`
        AND `day` `is on or after` (YMD 2010 5 4)
    WHEN `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` THEN
            `Part 5 Division 2 applies to the conveyance (s 88A)` `c`
        AND `day` `is before` (YMD 2019 2 8)
    WHERE
        `day` MEANS `c`'s `the date first executed`

-- s 102: the home concessions as they stood before 4 May 2010 are not in the reprint.
`the first day of the deposited home concessions (s 102)` MEANS YMD 2010 5 4

§§ `s 90AA -- qualifying home and established home`

-- s 90(10): "qualifying home means ... (a) for a conveyance that was first executed before 4 December 2012 -- a home;
-- (b) ... on or after 4 December 2012 but before 13 May 2014 -- a new home as defined in section 18(5) of the First Home
-- Owner Grant Act 2000 (as then in force); (c) ... on or after 13 May 2014 -- a qualifying home as defined in section
-- 90AA." s 90AA(1): "(a) the home has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence; or (b) ... a taxable
-- supply as a sale of new residential premises [GST Act s 40-75(1)(b), substantial renovation] ... (iii) the home has
-- not, since being renovated, been occupied or sold as a place of residence; or (c) the Commissioner declares the home
-- to be a qualifying home under subsection (2)." For (b) of s 90(10) the FHOG Act s 18(5) as then in force is not
-- deposited; INFERENCE: it is read as a home not previously occupied or sold as a place of residence.
-- s 88(1): "established home means a home that is not a qualifying home as defined in section 90AA."
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home is a qualifying home under s 90AA` IF
        `c`'s `the home has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`
    OR  `c`'s `the home is substantially renovated new residential premises not occupied or sold since`
    OR  `c`'s `the Commissioner declares the home a qualifying home`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home is a qualifying home for s 90` IF
    IF (`c`'s `the date first executed`) `is before` (YMD 2012 12 4)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF (`c`'s `the date first executed`) `is before` (YMD 2014 5 13)
         THEN `c`'s `the home has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`
         ELSE `the home is a qualifying home under s 90AA` `c`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the home is an established home` IF
    NOT (`the home is a qualifying home under s 90AA` `c`)

§§ `The conditions of each concession`

-- Common to every concession: the conveyees acquire the land outright, for themselves, and take possession in time.
-- ss 89(1)(f)-(h), (k); 89AA(2)(f)-(h), (j); 89AAB(2)(e)-(g), (i); 89A(1)(d)-(f), (i); 90(1)(c)-(e), (g).
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyees take the whole land for themselves, with possession in time` IF
        (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee already has a beneficial interest in the land`))
    AND `c`'s `the conveyees will acquire the whole beneficial interest in the land`
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee will acquire an interest in the land as trustee`))
    AND `c`'s `the conveyees become entitled to possession within 12 months after settlement`

-- s 89(1)(j), s 89A(1)(h): "(i) if at the relevant time there is a home on the land or the conveyance is an
-- off-the-plan contract -- the dutiable value of the land does not exceed $750 000; (ii) if at the relevant time there
-- is no home on the land -- the dutiable value of the land does not exceed $385 000".
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dutiable value is within the $750 000 or $385 000 cap` IF
    IF `c`'s `there is a home on the land at the relevant time` OR `c`'s `it is an off-the-plan contract`
    THEN `the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c` AT MOST 750000
    ELSE `the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c` AT MOST 385000

-- s 89(1): "(a) the conveyee or each of the conveyees is an individual; and (b) ... at least one of the conveyees is,
-- at least 18 years of age at the relevant time; and (c) ... at least one of the conveyees, is an Australian citizen or
-- a permanent resident ...; and (d) no conveyee and no spouse of a conveyee at the relevant time has previously received
-- the first home owner concession ...; and (e) no conveyee, and no spouse ..., has previously had a relevant interest in
-- a residential property that was occupied by the conveyee or spouse as a residence; ... (i) the conveyee or conveyees
-- will occupy a home on the land or to be built on the land as their principal place of residence for the prescribed
-- period commencing within the period for occupancy; and (j) [the cap]". READING: "the conveyee or conveyees will
-- occupy" requires each conveyee to occupy (s 90(8A) had to be added to relax the same words in s 90).
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 89(1) conditions are met` IF
        `c`'s `every conveyee is an individual`
    AND `c`'s `at least one conveyee is 18 or older, or is exempted from the age requirement`
    AND `c`'s `at least one conveyee is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee or spouse has received the first home owner concession before`))
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in a residence they occupied`))
    AND `the conveyees take the whole land for themselves, with possession in time` `c`
    AND (`c`'s `every conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence` OR `c`'s `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`)
    AND `the dutiable value is within the $750 000 or $385 000 cap` `c`

-- s 89AA(2): "(a) the conveyee is an individual; (b) ... at least 18 ...; (c) ... an Australian citizen, or a permanent
-- resident ...; (d) neither the conveyee, nor a spouse ..., has previously received any of the following: (i) a first
-- home owner grant; (ii) the first home owner discount; (iii) the first home owner concession; (iv) the senior,
-- pensioner and carer concession; (v) the principal place of residence rebate; (vi) a corresponding grant ...;
-- (e) neither ... has previously had a relevant interest in a residential property; ... (i) ... will occupy an
-- established home on the land as the conveyee's principal place of residence ...; (k) the conveyee is not entitled
-- to, and will not become entitled to, a first home owner grant". (3): (d) does not apply if the grant was repaid or
-- the duty paid. (12): (b), (c) and (i) are met if at least one conveyee meets them; (g) is read of the conveyees
-- together.
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 89AA(2) conditions are met` IF
        `c`'s `every conveyee is an individual`
    AND `c`'s `at least one conveyee is 18 or older, or is exempted from the age requirement`
    AND `c`'s `at least one conveyee is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee or spouse has received a grant, discount, concession or rebate before, not repaid`))
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in residential property`))
    AND `the conveyees take the whole land for themselves, with possession in time` `c`
    AND `the home is an established home` `c`
    AND (`c`'s `at least one conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence` OR `c`'s `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`)
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee has been paid, is entitled to or will become entitled to a first home owner grant`))

-- s 89AAB(2): "(a) the conveyee is an individual; (b) ... at least 18 ...; (c) ... an Australian citizen, or a
-- permanent resident ...; (d) subject to subsections (11) and (12), neither the conveyee, nor a spouse of the conveyee
-- at the relevant time, had a relevant interest in residential property in the Territory within 24 months before the
-- relevant time; ... (h) ... will occupy a home on the land as the conveyee's principal place of residence for the
-- prescribed period commencing within the period for occupancy". (16): (b), (c) and (h) are met if at least one
-- conveyee meets them. It is not limited to first home buyers. s 89AAC(1)-(2): if the conveyee is paid the first home
-- owner grant for an eligible transaction with a commencement date "on or after 1 January 2015 but before 7 May 2019",
-- for a conveyance first executed on or after 8 February 2019 at or under the threshold amount, "the person is not
-- eligible for the Territory home owner discount".
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 89AAB(2) conditions are met` IF
        `c`'s `every conveyee is an individual`
    AND `c`'s `at least one conveyee is 18 or older, or is exempted from the age requirement`
    AND `c`'s `at least one conveyee is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`
    AND (    (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee or spouse had a relevant interest in Territory residential property in the 24 months before`))
         OR  `c`'s `the Commissioner exempts that Territory interest for a relationship breakdown`)
    AND `the conveyees take the whole land for themselves, with possession in time` `c`
    AND (`c`'s `at least one conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence` OR `c`'s `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`)

GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 89AAC(2) excludes the Territory home owner discount` IF
        `c`'s `the conveyee is paid the grant for a transaction that commenced from 1 January 2015 to 6 May 2019`
    AND `day` `is on or after` (YMD 2019 2 8)
    AND `the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c` AT MOST `the threshold amount`
    WHERE
        `day` MEANS `c`'s `the date first executed`

-- s 89A(1): "(a) all the conveyees are individuals; and (b) at least 1 conveyee: (i) at the relevant time, is 60 years
-- of age or older; or (ii) ... is the eligible holder of an NT Pensioner and Carer Concession Card or a Northern
-- Territory Concession Scheme Card; or (iii) ... ; ... (g) the conveyees will occupy a home on the land ... as their
-- principal place of residence ...; (ga) the conveyee or conveyees have not been paid, are not entitled to, and will
-- not become entitled to, a first home owner grant ...; (h) [the cap]". (11AA): a conveyee is exempt from (g) if the
-- conveyance is first executed on or after 28 April 2015 and another conveyee "complies with the requirements in both
-- subsections (1)(b) and (g)". So before 28 April 2015 each conveyee must occupy; from then, one conveyee who meets
-- (b) is enough.
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 89A(1) conditions are met` IF
        `c`'s `every conveyee is an individual`
    AND (`c`'s `at least one conveyee is 60 or older at the relevant time` OR `c`'s `at least one conveyee holds an NT pensioner, carer or concession scheme card`)
    AND `the conveyees take the whole land for themselves, with possession in time` `c`
    AND (   `c`'s `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`
         OR (IF (`c`'s `the date first executed`) `is on or after` (YMD 2015 4 28)
             THEN `c`'s `a conveyee who is 60 or older or holds a card will occupy the home`
             ELSE `c`'s `every conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence`))
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee has been paid, is entitled to or will become entitled to a first home owner grant`))
    AND `the dutiable value is within the $750 000 or $385 000 cap` `c`

-- s 90(1): "(a) the conveyee or each of the conveyees is an individual; ... (f) the conveyee or conveyees will occupy a
-- qualifying home on the land or to be built on the land as their principal place of residence ...; (fa) the conveyee
-- or conveyees have not been paid, are not entitled to, and will not become entitled to, a first home owner grant ...".
-- (8A): from 28 April 2015 a conveyee is exempt from (f) if another conveyee complies with it. No value cap.
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 90(1) conditions are met` IF
        `c`'s `every conveyee is an individual`
    AND `the conveyees take the whole land for themselves, with possession in time` `c`
    AND `the home is a qualifying home for s 90` `c`
    AND (   `c`'s `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`
         OR (IF (`c`'s `the date first executed`) `is on or after` (YMD 2015 4 28)
             THEN `c`'s `at least one conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence`
             ELSE `c`'s `every conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence`))
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee has been paid, is entitled to or will become entitled to a first home owner grant`))

-- The s 88(1) definitions themselves limit two concessions by value. The Territory home owner discount is a concession
-- "(b) that applies if the dutiable value of the land does not exceed the threshold amount". The first home owner
-- discount has an amount only in the three limbs of its definition; from 1 January 2017 a conveyance above the threshold
-- amount falls in none of them, so there is no discount to be entitled to (NOTES.md).
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 88(1) definition of the first home owner discount gives an amount` IF
        `the day falls from` `day` `to` (YMD 2016 5 24) `and` (YMD 2016 8 31)
    OR  (`the day falls from` `day` `to` (YMD 2016 9 1) `and` (YMD 2019 5 6) AND `the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c` AT MOST `the threshold amount`)
    OR  (`the day falls from` `day` `to` (YMD 2016 9 1) `and` (YMD 2016 12 31) AND `the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c` GREATER THAN `the threshold amount`)
    WHERE
        `day` MEANS `c`'s `the date first executed`

-- Entitlement apart from s 90B: inside the date window and every condition met. READING (s 90AB): the Territory home
-- owner discount does not survive the payment of a first home owner grant for the conveyance or the home -- s 89AAC
-- denies it at the outset for the grants it names, and s 90AB(2) obliges the Commissioner to reassess it away once the
-- grant is paid. So a conveyee who has been or will be paid the grant is not counted as entitled to it.
GIVEN `the concession` IS A `Home concession`
      `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyees are entitled to` IF
        `the concession's date window includes the conveyance` `the concession` `c`
    AND CONSIDER `the concession`
        WHEN `the first home owner concession (s 89)` THEN `the s 89(1) conditions are met` `c`
        WHEN `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` THEN
                `the s 89AA(2) conditions are met` `c`
            AND `the s 88(1) definition of the first home owner discount gives an amount` `c`
        WHEN `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` THEN
                `the s 89AAB(2) conditions are met` `c`
            AND `the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c` AT MOST `the threshold amount`
            AND (NOT (`s 89AAC(2) excludes the Territory home owner discount` `c`))
            AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee has been paid, is entitled to or will become entitled to a first home owner grant`))
        WHEN `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` THEN `the s 89A(1) conditions are met` `c`
        WHEN `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` THEN `the s 90(1) conditions are met` `c`

§§ `s 90B -- one concession only, the one of greatest benefit`

-- s 90B(1)-(2): a conveyee who "would be entitled to more than one" of the five "is entitled to only one". (3): "(a) the
-- concession that gives the conveyee the greater or greatest benefit; or (b) if each concession gives the same benefit,
-- the concession determined by the Commissioner." s 113: s 90B applies to all conveyances, whenever executed.
DECLARE `Concession and amount` HAS
    `which` IS A `Home concession`
    `amount` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Concession choice` IS ONE OF
    `no Part 5 Division 2 concession: the Division does not apply to a conveyance first executed after 30 June 2021 (s 88A)`
    `no Part 5 Division 2 concession: the conditions of none of them are met`
    `the conveyee is entitled to` HAS `the concession` IS A `Home concession`, `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `concessions of equal benefit: the Commissioner determines which (s 90B(3)(b))` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the concession is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
      `the duty assessed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Concession and amount`
`the concessions the conveyees would be entitled to apart from s 90B` MEANS
    map (GIVEN `k` YIELD `Concession and amount` WITH `which` IS `k`, `amount` IS `the amount of` `k` `c` `the duty assessed`)
        (filter (GIVEN `k` YIELD `the conveyees are entitled to` `k` `c`) `all the home concessions`)

GIVEN `the list` IS A LIST OF `Concession and amount`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greatest amount in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the list`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `x` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN `the greater of` (`x`'s `amount`) (`the greatest amount in` `rest`)

GIVEN `the list` IS A LIST OF `Concession and amount`
      `the top` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Concession and amount`
`the concessions giving` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN `x` YIELD `x`'s `amount` EQUALS `the top`) `the list`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
      `the duty assessed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Concession choice`
`the s 90B choice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the concessions giving` `entitled` `top`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN
        IF `Part 5 Division 2 applies to the conveyance (s 88A)` `c` OR `READING: s 89AAB(1) is an express provision displacing s 88A`
        THEN `no Part 5 Division 2 concession: the conditions of none of them are met`
        ELSE `no Part 5 Division 2 concession: the Division does not apply to a conveyance first executed after 30 June 2021 (s 88A)`
    WHEN `x` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        CONSIDER `rest`
        WHEN EMPTY THEN `the conveyee is entitled to` (`x`'s `which`) (`x`'s `amount`)
        OTHERWISE `concessions of equal benefit: the Commissioner determines which (s 90B(3)(b))` `top`
    WHERE
        `entitled` MEANS `the concessions the conveyees would be entitled to apart from s 90B` `c` `the duty assessed`
        `top` MEANS `the greatest amount in` `entitled`

§§ `ss 90A and 90AB -- reassessment when the first home owner grant is paid, or is not (regulative)`

-- s 90A(1)-(2): if duty was assessed with the senior, pensioner and carer concession or the principal place of
-- residence rebate "and (b) the Commissioner subsequently authorises payment ... of a first home owner grant", the
-- Commissioner "must reassess duty on the conveyance on the basis that the conveyee or conveyees were not entitled" to
-- it. (3)-(4): if duty was assessed without it "because they would become entitled to a first home owner grant" and
-- they "do not become entitled", the Commissioner "must reassess ... if: (a) the conveyee or conveyees apply for the
-- reassessment; or (b) the Commissioner considers the reassessment appropriate". (5): both "apply even if the time limit
-- for reassessment under the Taxation Administration Act 2007 has passed". (6): the grant may be credited against the
-- duty. s 90AB(1)-(2): the same as s 90A(2) for the Territory home owner discount -- but s 90AB has no counterpart of
-- s 90A(5), so its reassessment stays inside the 5-year limit of TAA s 21(4) (NOTES.md). No period is stated for the
-- Commissioner to act, so the rules have no WITHIN.
GIVEN `the concession duty was assessed with` IS A `Home concession`
      `the Commissioner later authorises payment of the first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner must reassess without the concession once the grant is paid` IF
        `the Commissioner later authorises payment of the first home owner grant`
    AND CONSIDER `the concession duty was assessed with`
        WHEN `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the concession duty was assessed with` IS A `Home concession`
      `the Commissioner later authorises payment of the first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `ss 90A(2), 90AB(2) -- a grant paid after the concession means a reassessment without it` IS
    IF `the Commissioner must reassess without the concession once the grant is paid` `the concession duty was assessed with` `the Commissioner later authorises payment of the first home owner grant`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `reassess duty on the conveyance without the concession`
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN `duty was assessed without the concession because the grant was expected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conveyees do not become entitled to the grant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conveyees apply, or the Commissioner considers it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 90A(4) -- no grant after all means a reassessment with the concession` IS
    IF      `duty was assessed without the concession because the grant was expected`
        AND `the conveyees do not become entitled to the grant`
        AND `the conveyees apply, or the Commissioner considers it appropriate`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `reassess duty on the conveyance with the concession`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `The period for occupancy and the prescribed period (s 88(1))`

-- s 88(1) "period for occupancy": "(a) if the home is built on the land at the relevant time -- 12 months after the date
-- the conveyees become entitled to possession of the land under the conveyance; or (b) if there is no home built on the
-- land at the relevant time and the conveyees are owner builders of the home or have entered into a comprehensive home
-- building contract for the home -- the earlier of ...: (i) 5 years after the date the conveyees become entitled to
-- possession of the land; (ii) 12 months after completion of the building of the home; or (c) if there is no home ...
-- and the conveyees have entered into an off-the-plan contract ... -- 12 months after the date the conveyees become
-- entitled to possession ...; or (d) in any case -- the longer period approved by the Commissioner". Counted here in
-- months after the conveyees become entitled to possession. "prescribed period means: (a) a continuous period of 6
-- months; or (b) a shorter continuous period approved by the Commissioner". s 90C(3) applies these to Division 2A.
DECLARE `The home at the relevant time` IS ONE OF
    `a home is built on the land`
    `no home yet: the conveyees are owner builders or have a comprehensive home building contract`
    `no home yet: the conveyees have an off-the-plan contract`

GIVEN `the home` IS A `The home at the relevant time`
      `months from possession to completion of the home` IS A NUMBER
      `a longer period approved by the Commissioner, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the period for occupancy, in months after possession` MEANS
    `the greater of` `by the Act` `a longer period approved by the Commissioner, in months`
    WHERE
        `by the Act` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the home`
            WHEN `a home is built on the land` THEN 12
            WHEN `no home yet: the conveyees are owner builders or have a comprehensive home building contract` THEN
                `the lesser of` 60 (`months from possession to completion of the home` PLUS 12)
            WHEN `no home yet: the conveyees have an off-the-plan contract` THEN 12

`the prescribed period, in months` MEANS 6

§§ `The notice of failure to occupy, and the Commissioner's reassessment (regulative)`

-- ss 89(3), 89AA(6), 89AAB(7), 89A(3), 90(3), 90D(5): the conveyee who fails, or will fail, to occupy the home as
-- required "must, within 30 days after the date on which it first becomes apparent that the failure will occur, give
-- written notice to the Commissioner of the failure or impending failure. Maximum penalty: 50 penalty units." Each note:
-- the subsection "does not apply to a conveyee who has an exemption from the relevant occupancy requirement". With
-- several conveyees: ss 89AA(12)(d)-(e), 89AAB(16)(d)-(e) and 90D(6): notice is needed only if ALL the conveyees fail,
-- and only one need give it; s 89A(3) is put on each conveyee who fails (with the s 89A(11AA) exemption); ss 89(3) and
-- 90(3) speak of "the conveyee or conveyees" and are read as engaged when the occupancy condition fails.
-- The Commissioner then "must, even though the time limit for reassessment under the Taxation Administration Act 2007
-- may have passed, reassess duty on the conveyance on the basis that the conveyee or conveyees were not eligible ...
-- unless, in the Commissioner's opinion, there are special reasons for not making the reassessment": ss 89(4),
-- 89AAB(4)(b), 89A(6)-(7), 90(4), 90D(8). s 89AA has no such subsection: the first home owner discount is recovered, if
-- at all, by an ordinary reassessment within TAA s 21(4). The value of a penalty unit is set by the Penalty Units Act,
-- not deposited: the penalty is stated in penalty units.
-- Clock: days from the day it first becomes apparent that the failure will occur.
DECLARE `Occupancy provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 89(3) -- first home owner concession`
    `s 89AA(6) -- first home owner discount`
    `s 89AAB(7) -- Territory home owner discount`
    `s 89A(3) -- senior, pensioner and carer concession`
    `s 90(3) -- principal place of residence rebate`
    `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor`

`the days to notify a failure to occupy` MEANS 30
`the maximum penalty for not notifying, in penalty units` MEANS 50

DECLARE `Occupancy failure` HAS
    `this conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `every conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `another conveyee has already given the notice`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `this conveyee has an exemption from the occupancy requirement`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the failure has occurred`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is of the opinion there are special reasons not to reassess` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the provision` IS AN `Occupancy provision`
      `f` IS AN `Occupancy failure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyee must give notice of the failure to occupy` IF
        (NOT (`f`'s `this conveyee has an exemption from the occupancy requirement`))
    AND CONSIDER `the provision`
        WHEN `s 89AA(6) -- first home owner discount` THEN `all fail, and no one has told the Commissioner`
        WHEN `s 89AAB(7) -- Territory home owner discount` THEN `all fail, and no one has told the Commissioner`
        WHEN `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` THEN `all fail, and no one has told the Commissioner`
        OTHERWISE `f`'s `this conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`
    WHERE
        `all fail, and no one has told the Commissioner` MEANS
                `f`'s `every conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`
            AND (NOT (`f`'s `another conveyee has already given the notice`))

GIVEN `the provision` IS AN `Occupancy provision`
      `f` IS AN `Occupancy failure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner must reassess after the failure to occupy` IF
        `f`'s `the failure has occurred`
    AND (NOT (`f`'s `the Commissioner is of the opinion there are special reasons not to reassess`))
    AND CONSIDER `the provision`
        WHEN `s 89AA(6) -- first home owner discount` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `s 89A(3) -- senior, pensioner and carer concession` THEN
            NOT (`f`'s `this conveyee has an exemption from the occupancy requirement`)
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the provision` IS AN `Occupancy provision`
      `f` IS AN `Occupancy failure`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `the notice of failure to occupy, and the reassessment that follows` IS
        (IF `the conveyee must give notice of the failure to occupy` `the provision` `f`
         THEN PARTY `the conveyee`
              MUST  `give the Commissioner written notice of the failure to occupy`
              WITHIN `the days to notify a failure to occupy`
              LEST  BREACH BY `the conveyee` BECAUSE "ss 89(3), 89AA(6), 89AAB(7), 89A(3), 90(3), 90D(5): written notice of the failure or impending failure to occupy must be given to the Commissioner within 30 days after it first becomes apparent; maximum penalty 50 penalty units"
         ELSE FULFILLED)
    RAND
        (IF `the Commissioner must reassess after the failure to occupy` `the provision` `f`
         THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
              MUST  `reassess duty on the conveyance without the concession`
         ELSE FULFILLED)

§§ `Which Stamp Duty Act reassessments may be made after 5 years (for TAA s 21(4)(c))`

-- TAA s 21(4)(c) lifts the 5-year limit where "the taxation law under which the liability arose authorises the making
-- of a reassessment more than 5 years after the initial assessment". This Act does so in ss 56A(6), 89(3A), 89(4),
-- 89AAB(3), 89AAB(4), 89A(5), 89A(6), 90(3A), 90(4), 90A(5) and 90D(8) ("even though the time limit ... has passed").
-- Not in s 89AA, nor in s 90AB.
DECLARE `Reason for reassessing` IS ONE OF
    `a failure to occupy the home (ss 89(4), 89AAB(4), 89A(6), 90(4), 90D(8))`
    `to give a home concession the conveyees would otherwise receive (ss 89(3A), 89AAB(3), 89A(5), 90(3A))`
    `the first home owner grant, after the senior, pensioner and carer concession or the rebate (s 90A)`
    `the first home owner grant, after the Territory home owner discount (s 90AB)`
    `a sub-sale after a refund or remission (s 56A(5), (6))`
    `a failure to occupy after the first home owner discount (s 89AA)`
    `any other reason`

GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Reason for reassessing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Stamp Duty Act authorises the reassessment after 5 years` IF
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `the first home owner grant, after the Territory home owner discount (s 90AB)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a failure to occupy after the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any other reason` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Part 5 Division 2A -- the exemption for a new home bought from a building contractor (ss 90C, 90D)`

-- s 90D(1): the section "applies in relation to a conveyance first executed during the period commencing on 1 July 2022
-- and ending on 30 June 2027 unless: (a) the conveyance replaces an earlier conveyance, first executed before 1 July
-- 2022 ...; or (b) ... the conveyee entered into an option to purchase before 1 July 2022; or (c) the conveyor ... had
-- an option, granted before 1 July 2022, to require the conveyee to purchase". (2): "The conveyance is exempt from duty
-- if all of the following conditions are met: (a) the conveyee is: (i) an individual; and (ii) subject to subsection (7),
-- at least 18 years of age at the relevant time; and (iii) an Australian citizen or a permanent resident at the relevant
-- time; (b) in the conveyance, the conveyee agrees to acquire title to and the whole beneficial interest in land owned by
-- a building contractor; (c) the conveyee has no beneficial interest in the land being conveyed before the relevant
-- time; (d) ... the building contractor agrees to convey the land to the conveyee; (e) ... the building contractor
-- agrees to ... (i) build or place a detached, new home on the land ...; (ii) complete the building of a partially
-- completed and detached, new home ...; (iii) convey a completed and detached, new home ...; (f) the land ... is owned
-- by the building contractor immediately before the conveyance is executed or will be ... immediately before settlement
-- ...; (g) the land ... was purchased by the building contractor from another person who developed it as a residential
-- lot; (h) the building contractor paid duty on the dutiable value of the land when the building contractor purchased
-- it from the person who developed it ...; (i) the conveyee occupies the home as the conveyee's principal place of
-- residence for the prescribed period commencing within the period for occupancy, unless the Commissioner is satisfied
-- that special reasons exist to vary this requirement; (j) the conveyee becomes entitled to possession of the land within
-- 12 months after settlement ...". (3): with 2 or more conveyees, at least one meets (a)(ii), at least one meets
-- (a)(iii), "all conditions in subsection (2) are met" and all agree to acquire title and the whole beneficial interest.
-- There is no cap on value and no first-home condition. Division 2A is not "this Division" of s 88A, so s 88A does not
-- close it; s 90C(3) borrows only the s 88(1) definitions. READING (NOTES.md): (3)(c) is read as requiring each
-- conveyee to occupy, though s 90D(6) asks for notice only when all fail.
DECLARE `New home from a building contractor` HAS
    `it replaces a conveyance first executed before 1 July 2022, or rests on an option granted before then` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conveyees agree to acquire title to and the whole beneficial interest in land owned by a building contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building contractor agrees to convey the land to the conveyees`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building contractor agrees to build, place, complete or convey a detached, new home on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building contractor owns the land before execution, or will before settlement`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building contractor bought the land from the person who developed it as a residential lot`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building contractor paid duty on the land's dutiable value when buying it from the developer` IS A BOOLEAN

`the first day of the s 90D window` MEANS YMD 2022 7 1
`the last day of the s 90D window` MEANS YMD 2027 6 30

GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
      `b` IS A `New home from a building contractor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyance is exempt under s 90D` IF
        `the day falls from` (`c`'s `the date first executed`) `to` `the first day of the s 90D window` `and` `the last day of the s 90D window`
    AND (NOT (`b`'s `it replaces a conveyance first executed before 1 July 2022, or rests on an option granted before then`))
    AND `c`'s `every conveyee is an individual`
    AND `c`'s `at least one conveyee is 18 or older, or is exempted from the age requirement`
    AND `c`'s `at least one conveyee is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`
    AND `b`'s `the conveyees agree to acquire title to and the whole beneficial interest in land owned by a building contractor`
    AND (NOT (`c`'s `a conveyee already has a beneficial interest in the land`))
    AND `b`'s `the building contractor agrees to convey the land to the conveyees`
    AND `b`'s `the building contractor agrees to build, place, complete or convey a detached, new home on the land`
    AND `b`'s `the building contractor owns the land before execution, or will before settlement`
    AND `b`'s `the building contractor bought the land from the person who developed it as a residential lot`
    AND `b`'s `the building contractor paid duty on the land's dutiable value when buying it from the developer`
    AND (`c`'s `every conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence` OR `c`'s `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`)
    AND `c`'s `the conveyees become entitled to possession within 12 months after settlement`

§§ `Part 5 Division 3 -- property settlements on the breakdown of a relationship (s 91)`

-- s 91(1): exempt if "(a) the parties to the conveyance are or were parties to a marriage or de facto relationship under
-- the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth); and (b) within 12 months after the date of the conveyance, an order is made by the
-- Family Court for the distribution of property between the parties ... under Part VIII or VIIIAB ...; and (c) the
-- terms of the conveyance are consistent with the order." (2): the same for "a binding financial agreement ... under
-- Part VIIIA or VIIIAB", where "(b) the conveyance occurred after the irretrievable breakdown". (3): "Except as
-- otherwise provided by the Taxation Administration Act 2007, the Commissioner must refund any duty paid on a conveyance
-- before it becomes exempt".
DECLARE `Settlement instrument` IS ONE OF
    `a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act`
    `a binding financial agreement under Part VIIIA or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act`
    `no order or agreement yet`

DECLARE `Relationship settlement` HAS
    `the parties are or were married or in a de facto relationship under the Family Law Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the conveyance`                                                            IS A DATE
    `the instrument`                                                                        IS A `Settlement instrument`
    `the date the order was made or the agreement was made`                                 IS A DATE
    `the conveyance occurred after the relationship irretrievably broke down`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the terms of the conveyance are consistent with the order or agreement`                IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `s` IS A `Relationship settlement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyance is exempt under s 91` IF
        `s`'s `the parties are or were married or in a de facto relationship under the Family Law Act`
    AND `the day falls from` (`s`'s `the date the order was made or the agreement was made`) `to` (`s`'s `the date of the conveyance`) `and` (`years after` 1 (`s`'s `the date of the conveyance`))
    AND `s`'s `the terms of the conveyance are consistent with the order or agreement`
    AND CONSIDER `s`'s `the instrument`
        WHEN `a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a binding financial agreement under Part VIIIA or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` THEN
            `s`'s `the conveyance occurred after the relationship irretrievably broke down`
        WHEN `no order or agreement yet` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `s` IS A `Relationship settlement`
      `duty was paid before the conveyance became exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner must refund the duty under s 91(3)` IF
    `the conveyance is exempt under s 91` `s` AND `duty was paid before the conveyance became exempt`

GIVEN `s` IS A `Relationship settlement`
      `duty was paid before the conveyance became exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 91(3) -- the Commissioner must refund duty paid before the conveyance became exempt` IS
    IF `the Commissioner must refund the duty under s 91(3)` `s` `duty was paid before the conveyance became exempt`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `refund the duty paid`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Schedule 2 items 6(d), 6(e) and 7 -- exemptions an individual meets`

-- Schedule 2 item 6: "Conveyance: ... (d) made by a trustee as executor of the will, or administrator of the estate, of
-- a deceased person, to a beneficiary of the deceased person's estate in accordance with the provisions of the will or
-- the rules of intestate distribution; or (e) in relation to which the Commissioner is satisfied of both of the
-- following: (i) no valuable consideration is given for the conveyance; (ii) the conveyance is made to a Special
-- Disability Trust as defined in the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) or Veterans Entitlement Act 1986 (Cth)."
GIVEN `made by the executor or administrator to a beneficiary under the will or the intestacy rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyance is exempt under Schedule 2 item 6(d)` IF
    `made by the executor or administrator to a beneficiary under the will or the intestacy rules`

GIVEN `no valuable consideration is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conveyance is to a Special Disability Trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyance is exempt under Schedule 2 item 6(e)` IF
    `no valuable consideration is given` AND `the conveyance is to a Special Disability Trust`

-- Schedule 2 item 7: "Conveyance where the Commissioner is satisfied that: (a) there are 2 parties to the conveyance and
-- each is the spouse of the other; and (b) the property subject to the conveyance is the principal place of residence
-- of the parties ...; and (c) no consideration is given ...; and (d) the effect of the conveyance is that both parties
-- ... will own the place of residence ... in equal shares; and (e) no other person takes an interest under the
-- conveyance." s 4(1): "spouse includes de facto partner".
DECLARE `Transfer between spouses` HAS
    `there are 2 parties and each is the spouse or de facto partner of the other` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the property is the parties' principal place of residence`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `no consideration is given`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `both will own the home in equal shares`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `no other person takes an interest`                                        IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transfer between spouses`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyance is exempt under Schedule 2 item 7` IF
        `t`'s `there are 2 parties and each is the spouse or de facto partner of the other`
    AND `t`'s `the property is the parties' principal place of residence`
    AND `t`'s `no consideration is given`
    AND `t`'s `both will own the home in equal shares`
    AND `t`'s `no other person takes an interest`

§§ `The duty on a home conveyance`

-- The duty assessed under Schedule 1, or `not covered` before the deposited Schedule 1 applies.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the Schedule 1 duty on a conveyance first executed on` MEANS
    IF `the deposited Schedule 1 applies on` `the day`
    THEN `the duty, in dollars, is` (`the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` `the dutiable value`)
    ELSE `not covered` `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the dutiable value of the interest not retained` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the Schedule 1 cl 1(3) duty on a joint tenancy conveyance first executed on` MEANS
    IF `the deposited Schedule 1 applies on` `the day`
    THEN `the duty, in dollars, is` (`the Schedule 1 cl 1(3) duty on a joint tenancy conveyance` `the dutiable value of the interest not retained`)
    ELSE `not covered` `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the Schedule 1 duty on the conveyance` MEANS
    `the Schedule 1 duty on a conveyance first executed on` (`c`'s `the date first executed`) (`the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c`)

-- s 90B applied to the duty assessed, or `not covered`.
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
GIVETH A `Concession choice`
`the home concession for the conveyance` MEANS
    IF `the deposited Schedule 1 applies on` (`c`'s `the date first executed`)
    THEN `the s 90B choice` `c` (`the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` (`the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c`))
    ELSE `the concession is not covered` `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`

GIVEN `the choice` IS A `Concession choice`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the concession amount in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the choice`
    WHEN `the conveyee is entitled to` `k` `amount` THEN `amount`
    WHEN `concessions of equal benefit: the Commissioner determines which (s 90B(3)(b))` `amount` THEN `amount`
    OTHERWISE 0

-- The duty payable: nil if the s 90D exemption applies; otherwise the Schedule 1 duty less the s 90B concession, rounded
-- down to a multiple of 5 cents (TAA s 27).
GIVEN `c` IS A `Home conveyance`
      `b` IS A `New home from a building contractor`
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the duty payable on the home conveyance` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the deposited Schedule 1 applies on` (`c`'s `the date first executed`)))
    THEN `the Schedule 1 duty on the conveyance` `c`
    ELSE IF `the conveyance is exempt under s 90D` `c` `b`
         THEN `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
         ELSE `the duty, in dollars, is`
                  (`rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents`
                      (`assessed` MINUS `the concession amount in` (`the home concession for the conveyance` `c`)))
    WHERE
        `assessed` MEANS `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` (`the dutiable value of the conveyance` `c`)
